# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Étape 1 : Transposer les entrées classiques en un problème quantique {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hamiltonian and reference state {#hamiltonian-and-reference-state}"
msgstr "Hamiltonien et état de référence {#hamiltonian-and-reference-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example uses a 12-qubit open-boundary Heisenberg chain ($n=12$),\n"
msgstr "Cet exemple utilise une chaîne de Heisenberg à limites ouvertes de 12 qubits ($n=12$),\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\left(X_iX_{i+1}+Y_iY_{i+1}+Z_iZ_{i+1}\\right),\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\left(X_iX_{i+1}+Y_iY_{i+1}+Z_iZ_{i+1}\\right),\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with a single-excitation product state\n"
msgstr "avec un état produit à excitation unique\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=|000001000000\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=|000001000000\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"as the reference state.\n"
"Because the Heisenberg Hamiltonian defined above conserves the total number of excitations, the reference state stays in the single-excitation subspace, whose dimension grows only linearly with the number of qubits. We can therefore compute the exact ground-state energy efficiently, by diagonalizing the Hamiltonian restricted to that subspace, and use it purely as a diagnostic benchmark for the KQD estimate. The KQD workflow itself estimates projected matrix elements by using Qiskit primitives and solves the resulting projected problem classically.\n"
msgstr ""
"comme état de référence.\n"
"Étant donné que le hamiltonien de Heisenberg défini ci-dessus conserve le nombre total d'excitations, l'état de référence reste dans le sous-espace à excitation unique, dont la dimension croît uniquement de manière linéaire avec le nombre de qubits. Nous pouvons donc calculer efficacement l'énergie exacte de l'état fondamental, en diagonalisant le hamiltonien restreint à ce sous-espace, et l'utiliser purement comme référence de diagnostic pour l'estimation KQD. Le flux de travail KQD lui-même estime les éléments de matrice projetés à l'aide des primitives Qiskit et résout le problème projeté résultant de manière classique.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the parameters for the algorithm {#set-the-parameters-for-the-algorithm}"
msgstr "Définition des paramètres de l'algorithme {#set-the-parameters-for-the-algorithm}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Based on the upper-bounds on the Hamiltonian norm, Ref. [\\[1\\]](#references) heuristically suggests the time step $\\Delta t$ as $\\pi/\\|H\\|$.\n"
"Because the spectral norm $\\|H\\|$ is hard to compute, we instead use its upper bound:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sur la base des bornes supérieures de la norme du hamiltonien, la réf. [\\[1\\]](#references) suggère heuristiquement le pas de temps $\\Delta t$ comme $\\pi/\\|H\\|$.\n"
"Étant donné que la norme spectrale $\\|H\\|$ est difficile à calculer, nous utilisons à la place sa borne supérieure :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\|H\\| \\le \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\underbrace{\\|X_i X_{i+1}+Y_{i} Y_{i+1}+Z_{i} Z_{i+1}\\|}_{4 \\times 4 \\text{ matrix, easy to calculate the norm}} = 3(n-1).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\|H\\| \\le \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\underbrace{\\|X_i X_{i+1}+Y_{i} Y_{i+1}+Z_{i} Z_{i+1}\\|}_{4 \\times 4 \\text{ matrix, easy to calculate the norm}} = 3(n-1).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We set the Krylov dimension to $r=10$ and the number of Trotter steps per time step to $5$: a large enough Krylov space to resolve the low-lying spectrum while keeping the deepest circuit ($t_{\\max}=(r-1)\\Delta t$) affordable, and enough Trotter steps to keep the discretization error small at that deepest circuit.\n"
msgstr "Nous fixons la dimension de Krylov à $r=10$ et le nombre de pas de Trotter par pas de temps à $5$ : un espace de Krylov suffisamment grand pour résoudre le spectre de basse énergie tout en gardant le circuit le plus profond ($t_{\\max}=(r-1)\\Delta t$) abordable, et suffisamment de pas de Trotter pour maintenir une petite erreur de discrétisation à ce circuit le plus profond.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build circuit {#build-circuit}"
msgstr "Construire le circuit {#build-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we build the circuits to estimate the matrix elements $\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}$ and $\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}$.\n"
"Because all powers of $H$ commute, we have\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Ici, nous construisons les circuits pour estimer les éléments de matrice $\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}$ et $\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}$.\n"
"Étant donné que toutes les puissances de $H$ commutent, nous avons\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|H e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{H}_{0,\\ell-k},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|H e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{H}_{0,\\ell-k},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{S}_{0,\\ell-k}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"Such matrices where the elements depend on the index differences in this manner are called *Toeplitz* and can be reconstructed from first-row elements indexed by $d=\\ell-k$.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{S}_{0,\\ell-k}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"Such matrices where the elements depend on the index differences in this manner are called *Toeplitz* and can be reconstructed from first-row elements indexed by $d=\\ell-k$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we present the circuit, called **extended-swap-test**, which prepares\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle=\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle+|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where $|\\psi_d\\rangle=e^{-id\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ici, nous présentons le circuit, appelé **test de swap étendu**, qui prépare\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle=\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle+|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"où $|\\psi_d\\rangle=e^{-id\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reference state {#reference-state}"
msgstr "État de référence {#reference-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We prepare the reference state $|\\psi_0\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Nous préparons l'état de référence $|\\psi_0\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/fb2879c5-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/fb2879c5-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Time evolution {#time-evolution}"
msgstr "Évolution temporelle {#time-evolution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Realize the time-evolution operator generated by the Hamiltonian, approximated by simple [Lie-Trotterization](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter).\n"
msgstr "Réalise l'opérateur d'évolution temporelle généré par le hamiltonien, approximé par une simple [Lie-Trotterisation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter).\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/017b8548-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/017b8548-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extended swap test circuit [\\[3\\]](#references) {#extended-swap-test-circuit-3references}"
msgstr "Circuit de test de swap étendu [\\[3\\]](#references) {#extended-swap-test-circuit-3references}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit first prepares the reference state on the system register while the ancilla remains in $|0\\rangle$:\n"
msgstr "Le circuit prépare d'abord l'état de référence sur le registre système tandis que l'ancilla reste à $|0\\rangle$ :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_{0}\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_{0}\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then, applying a Hadamard gate to the ancilla creates a coherent superposition of two branches:\n"
msgstr "Ensuite, l'application d'une porte de Hadamard à l'ancilla crée une superposition cohérente de deux branches :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, the controlled time-evolution gate applies:\n"
msgstr "Enfin, la porte d'évolution temporelle contrôlée s'applique :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t=d\\Delta t) = e^{-id\\Delta t H}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t=d\\Delta t) = e^{-id\\Delta t H}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "only when the ancilla is in the $|1\\rangle$ branch. Therefore,\n"
msgstr "uniquement lorsque l'ancilla est dans la branche $|1\\rangle$. Par conséquent,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the next code block, we implement:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Psi(t)\\rangle = \\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"which will be assigned as $t=d\\Delta t$ for $d=1,\\cdots r-1$ in the execution step.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dans le prochain bloc de code, nous implémentons :\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Psi(t)\\rangle = \\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"qui sera assigné comme $t=d\\Delta t$ pour $d=1,\\cdots r-1$ à l'étape d'exécution.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/1260f66a-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/1260f66a-0.avif)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Observables {#observables}"
msgstr "Observables {#observables}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For any Hermitian system observable $O$, here we set the observables to calculate:\n"
msgstr "Pour tout observable hermitien du système $O$, nous fixons ici les observables à calculer :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"z=\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"z=\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is because $O=I$ gives the overlap element $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle$, while $O=H$ gives the Hamiltonian element $\\mathcal{H}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Cela s'explique par le fait que $O=I$ donne l'élément de recouvrement $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle$, tandis que $O=H$ donne l'élément du hamiltonien $\\mathcal{H}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using $X=|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$, we have\n"
msgstr "En utilisant $X=|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$, nous avons\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|X\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(X\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{z+z^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|X\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(X\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{z+z^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Re} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Re} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Similarly, using $Y=-i|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+i|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$,\n"
msgstr "De même, en utilisant $Y=-i|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+i|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(Y\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"-i\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"i\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{-iz+iz^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(Y\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"-i\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"i\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{-iz+iz^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Im} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Im} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, we have\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|X\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Par conséquent, nous avons\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|X\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Re}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Re}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Im}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Im}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, for each state $|\\Psi_{0d}\\rangle$, we need to measure:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"X \\otimes I \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes I \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"X \\otimes H \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{H}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes H \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{H}_{0d}.\\\\\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Enfin, pour chaque état $|\\Psi_{0d}\\rangle$, nous devons mesurer :\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"X \\otimes I \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes I \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"X \\otimes H \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{H}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes H \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{H}_{0d}.\\\\\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the estimation of the $\\mathcal{H}$ matrix elements, the number of Pauli terms is much larger than that for the $\\mathcal{S}$ matrix elements.\n"
msgstr "Pour l'estimation des éléments de matrice $\\mathcal{H}$, le nombre de termes de Pauli est bien plus grand que celui des éléments de matrice $\\mathcal{S}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can now reduce the number of measured Hamiltonian terms by using a shifting technique [\\[4\\]](#references).\n"
"We split the Hamiltonian as:\n"
msgstr ""
"Nous pouvons maintenant réduire le nombre de termes du hamiltonien mesurés en utilisant une technique de décalage [\\[4\\]](#references).\n"
"Nous décomposons le hamiltonien comme :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H = (H-T) + T,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H = (H-T) + T,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $T$ is chosen such that the reference state is its eigenstate,\n"
msgstr "où $T$ est choisi de sorte que l'état de référence en soit l'état propre,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then,\n"
msgstr "Then,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{0d}\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|T|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{0d}\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|T|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here,\n"
msgstr "Here,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is the shifted Hamiltonian matrix element.\n"
"Therefore, we only need to measure $X\\otimes (H-T)$ and $Y\\otimes (H-T)$.\n"
"The contribution from $T$ is reconstructed classically using the already measured overlap matrix element $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"est l'élément de matrice du hamiltonien décalé.\n"
"Par conséquent, nous n'avons besoin de mesurer que $X\\otimes (H-T)$ et $Y\\otimes (H-T)$.\n"
"La contribution de $T$ est reconstruite classiquement à l'aide de l'élément de matrice de recouvrement déjà mesuré $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this example, a natural choice is the diagonal part of the Heisenberg Hamiltonian,\n"
msgstr "Dans cet exemple, un choix naturel est la partie diagonale du hamiltonien de Heisenberg,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the reference state is a computational-basis state, it is an eigenstate of every $Z_iZ_{i+1}$ term.\n"
msgstr "Étant donné que l'état de référence est un état de la base computationnelle, il s'agit d'un état propre de chaque terme $Z_iZ_{i+1}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "However, a more advantageous choice is to include not only the diagonal $ZZ$ terms, but also the $XX+YY$ terms that annihilate the reference state.\n"
msgstr "Cependant, un choix plus avantageux consiste à inclure non seulement les termes diagonaux $ZZ$, mais aussi les termes $XX+YY$ qui annihilent l'état de référence.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each neighboring pair, the operator $XX+YY$ satisfies\n"
msgstr "Pour chaque paire voisine, l'opérateur $XX+YY$ satisfait\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|00\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|11\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|00\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|11\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and\n"
msgstr "and\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|01\\rangle = 2|10\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|10\\rangle = 2|01\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|01\\rangle = 2|10\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|10\\rangle = 2|01\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, the $XX+YY$ term contributes only when the two neighboring qubits have different occupations in the reference bitstring.\n"
"If the two qubits are both $0$ or both $1$, the term annihilates the reference state and can also be shifted out.\n"
msgstr ""
"Par conséquent, le terme $XX+YY$ ne contribue que lorsque les deux qubits voisins ont des occupations différentes dans le bitstring de référence.\n"
"Si les deux qubits sont tous deux $0$ ou tous deux $1$, le terme annihile l'état de référence et peut également être décalé.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let $|\\psi_{\\rm ref}\\rangle = |z_0\\cdots z_{n-1}\\rangle$, where $z_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$.\n"
"Thus, we can choose\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"\\sum_{z_i={z_{i+1}}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Soit $|\\psi_{\\rm ref}\\rangle = |z_0\\cdots z_{n-1}\\rangle$, où $z_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$.\n"
"Ainsi, nous pouvons choisir\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"\\sum_{z_i={z_{i+1}}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This operator still satisfies\n"
msgstr "Cet opérateur satisfait toujours\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"because the $ZZ$ terms act diagonally on $|\\psi_0\\rangle$, while the shifted $XX+YY$ terms give zero.\n"
"The corresponding eigenvalue is therefore determined only by the $ZZ$ terms,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\tau = \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\n"
"(-1)^{z_i}\n"
"(-1)^{z_{i+1}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"car les termes $ZZ$ agissent diagonalement sur $|\\psi_0\\rangle$, tandis que les termes décalés $XX+YY$ donnent zéro.\n"
"La valeur propre correspondante est donc déterminée uniquement par les termes $ZZ$,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\tau = \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\n"
"(-1)^{z_i}\n"
"(-1)^{z_{i+1}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With this choice, the shifted Hamiltonian becomes:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H-T = \\sum_{z_i\\ne z_{i+1}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Avec ce choix, le hamiltonien décalé devient :\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H-T = \\sum_{z_i\\ne z_{i+1}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a result, only the edges with different occupations in the reference state need to be measured.\n"
"All $ZZ$ terms and all inactive $XX+YY$ terms are reconstructed through the overlap contribution $\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}$, or give zero contribution by construction.\n"
msgstr ""
"En conséquence, seules les arêtes ayant des occupations différentes dans l'état de référence doivent être mesurées.\n"
"Tous les termes $ZZ$ et tous les termes $XX+YY$ inactifs sont reconstruits par le biais de la contribution de recouvrement $\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}$, ou donnent une contribution nulle par construction.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This gives a smaller observable than shifting only the diagonal part.\n"
"In particular, for a computational-basis reference state with a localized excitation, only the edges adjacent to the excitation remain in $H-T$.\n"
"Therefore, the number of Pauli terms in $X\\otimes(H-T)$ and $Y\\otimes(H-T)$ can be substantially reduced, while the reconstructed matrix element\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Cela donne un observable plus petit que le décalage de la seule partie diagonale.\n"
"En particulier, pour un état de référence de la base computationnelle avec une excitation localisée, seules les arêtes adjacentes à l'excitation restent dans $H-T$.\n"
"Par conséquent, le nombre de termes de Pauli dans $X\\otimes(H-T)$ et $Y\\otimes(H-T)$ peut être considérablement réduit, tandis que l'élément de matrice reconstruit\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "remains exactly the same.\n"
msgstr "reste exactement le même.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Étape 2 : Optimiser le problème pour l'exécution sur du matériel quantique {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we turn the abstract extended-swap-test circuit into a hardware-oriented template.\n"
"Before that, we further optimize the circuit in the abstract level first.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nous transformons maintenant le circuit abstrait de test de swap étendu en un modèle orienté matériel.\n"
"Avant cela, nous optimisons d'abord davantage le circuit au niveau abstrait.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare Hamiltonian term ordering {#compare-hamiltonian-term-ordering}"
msgstr "Comparer l'ordre des termes du hamiltonien {#compare-hamiltonian-term-ordering}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, we compare different orderings of the Pauli terms in the Heisenberg Hamiltonian for the Hamiltonian simulation.\n"
"The Hamiltonian itself is unchanged, but the ordering affects how the product-formula circuit is generated and how much the structure can be parallelized in the circuit.\n"
"For example, the naive ordering lists all nearest-neighbor $XX$ terms, then all $YY$ terms, then all $ZZ$ terms.\n"
"This places adjacent edges such as $(0,1)$ and $(1,2)$ next to each other, so they cannot be executed in parallel.\n"
"The even-then-odd ordering visits disjoint even edges first, followed by odd edges, which exposes parallel two-qubit layers.\n"
"The even-odd edge-grouped ordering goes one step further: for each edge, it keeps the local $XX$, $YY$, and $ZZ$ terms together, while still visiting even edges before odd edges.\n"
"We expect the even-then-odd and even-odd edge-grouped orderings to reduce circuit depth by exposing parallel two-qubit layers, and the edge-grouped ordering to additionally reduce the Trotter error because the local two-qubit interaction on the same edge is handled as a compact block.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tout d'abord, nous comparons différents ordres des termes de Pauli dans le hamiltonien de Heisenberg pour la simulation du hamiltonien.\n"
"Le hamiltonien lui-même reste inchangé, mais l'ordre affecte la façon dont le circuit à formule de produit est généré et la mesure dans laquelle la structure peut être parallélisée dans le circuit.\n"
"Par exemple, l'ordre naïf liste tous les termes $XX$ de plus proches voisins, puis tous les termes $YY$, puis tous les termes $ZZ$.\n"
"Cela place des arêtes adjacentes telles que $(0,1)$ et $(1,2)$ l'une à côté de l'autre, de sorte qu'elles ne peuvent pas être exécutées en parallèle.\n"
"L'ordre pair-puis-impair visite d'abord les arêtes paires disjointes, suivies des arêtes impaires, ce qui expose des couches à deux qubits parallèles.\n"
"L'ordre pair-impair groupé par arête va encore plus loin : pour chaque arête, il conserve ensemble les termes locaux $XX$, $YY$ et $ZZ$, tout en visitant toujours les arêtes paires avant les arêtes impaires.\n"
"Nous nous attendons à ce que les ordres pair-puis-impair et pair-impair groupé par arête réduisent la profondeur du circuit en exposant des couches à deux qubits parallèles, et à ce que l'ordre groupé par arête réduise en outre l'erreur de Trotter car l'interaction locale à deux qubits sur la même arête est traitée comme un bloc compact.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Pauli evolutions with different term ordering](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/ham_ordering.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Pauli evolutions with different term ordering](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/ham_ordering.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Hamiltonian ordering also affects the Trotter error.\n"
"If we place noncommuting terms next to each other, the basis transitions occur more often, which induces more Trotter error.\n"
"By grouping terms that require the same Pauli-basis transformation, redundant basis-changes can be avoided.\n"
msgstr ""
"L'ordre du hamiltonien affecte également l'erreur de Trotter.\n"
"Si nous plaçons des termes non commutants l'un à côté de l'autre, les transitions de base se produisent plus souvent, ce qui induit davantage d'erreur de Trotter.\n"
"En regroupant les termes qui nécessitent la même transformation de base de Pauli, on peut éviter des changements de base redondants.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, the comparison uses the largest evolution time that appears in the first-row Krylov estimates,\n"
"$t_{\\max} = (r-1)\\Delta t,$\n"
"using the same transpilation condition.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ici, la comparaison utilise le temps d'évolution le plus grand qui apparaît dans les estimations de Krylov de première ligne,\n"
"$t_{\\max} = (r-1)\\Delta t,$\n"
"en utilisant la même condition de transpilation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In order to measure the Trotter error, we use **process infidelity** between the Trotterized circuit and the exact Hamiltonian evolution,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\text{Infidelity}(U,V)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Afin de mesurer l'erreur de Trotter, nous utilisons l'**infidélité de processus** entre le circuit trotterisé et l'évolution exacte du hamiltonien,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\text{Infidelity}(U,V)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1-F(U,V)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"1-F(U,V)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1 - \\frac{|\\operatorname{Tr}(U^\\dagger V)|^2}{d^2},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where $d=2^n$ is the dimension of the Hilbert space.\n"
msgstr ""
"1 - \\frac{|\\operatorname{Tr}(U^\\dagger V)|^2}{d^2},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where $d=2^n$ is the dimension of the Hilbert space.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This diagnostic uses dense matrices, so it is suitable for this small 12-qubit example but not intended as a scalable subroutine.\n"
msgstr "Ce diagnostic utilise des matrices denses, il convient donc à ce petit exemple à 12 qubits mais n'est pas destiné à être une sous-routine évolutive.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We first keep the synthesis rule fixed to one first-order Trotter step and vary only the Pauli-term ordering.\n"
"The goal of this comparison is mainly to see how much circuit depth and two-qubit cost can be reduced by exposing disjoint nearest-neighbor edges to the transpiler.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nous fixons d'abord la règle de synthèse à un seul pas de Trotter du premier ordre et ne faisons varier que l'ordre des termes de Pauli.\n"
"L'objectif de cette comparaison est principalement de voir dans quelle mesure la profondeur du circuit et le coût en portes à deux qubits peuvent être réduits en exposant des arêtes disjointes de plus proches voisins au transpilateur.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-1.avif)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-3.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-3.avif)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-5.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-5.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At `reps=1`, we observe that even-then-odd and even-odd edge-grouped orderings both collapse the depth from 15 to 6 by exposing parallel two-qubit layers, while the two-qubit gate count stays the same across all three orderings.\n"
"However, all three orderings have infidelity close to 1, so we sweep the number of Trotter repetitions to separate the orderings more clearly.\n"
"As the number of repetitions grows, the infidelity of `even-odd edge-grouped` ordering drops faster than the other two, reaching 0.045 at `reps=8` versus 0.075 for naive and even-then-odd ordering.\n"
msgstr ""
"À `reps=1`, nous observons que les ordres pair-puis-impair et pair-impair groupé par arête font tous deux passer la profondeur de 15 à 6 en exposant des couches à deux qubits parallèles, tandis que le nombre de portes à deux qubits reste le même pour les trois ordres.\n"
"Cependant, les trois ordres ont une infidélité proche de 1, nous balayons donc le nombre de répétitions de Trotter pour mieux séparer les ordres.\n"
"À mesure que le nombre de répétitions augmente, l'infidélité de l'ordre `even-odd edge-grouped` chute plus rapidement que les deux autres, atteignant 0,045 à `reps=8` contre 0,075 pour l'ordre naïf et l'ordre pair-puis-impair.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare product-formula synthesis {#compare-product-formula-synthesis}"
msgstr "Comparer la synthèse par formule de produit {#compare-product-formula-synthesis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we explore different advanced settings of Trotterization, with the fixed Hamiltonian ordering to the even-odd edge-grouped ordering.\n"
"We consider first-order Lie-Trotter, second-order Suzuki-Trotter, and fourth-order Suzuki-Trotter.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ensuite, nous explorons différents paramètres avancés de la trotterisation, avec l'ordre du hamiltonien fixé à l'ordre pair-impair groupé par arête.\n"
"Nous considérons le Lie-Trotter du premier ordre, le Suzuki-Trotter du deuxième ordre et le Suzuki-Trotter du quatrième ordre.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Lie-Trotter gives the shallowest circuit but has the largest error, while the fourth-order Suzuki-Trotter is more accurate but increases the circuit depth.\n"
"For the rest of the tutorial, we choose second-order Suzuki-Trotter because it gives a small-depth circuit while substantially reducing the Trotter error relative to the first-order formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lie-Trotter donne le circuit le moins profond mais a la plus grande erreur, tandis que le Suzuki-Trotter du quatrième ordre est plus précis mais augmente la profondeur du circuit.\n"
"Pour le reste du tutoriel, nous choisissons le Suzuki-Trotter du deuxième ordre car il donne un circuit de faible profondeur tout en réduisant substantiellement l'erreur de Trotter par rapport à la formule du premier ordre.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remove the controlled time-evolution gate {#remove-the-controlled-time-evolution-gate}"
msgstr "Supprimer la porte d'évolution temporelle contrôlée {#remove-the-controlled-time-evolution-gate}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the extended swap test, controlling time evolution with a single ancilla qubit requires the ancilla to control many gates across the system.\n"
"This can introduce substantial routing overhead and, in the worst case, effectively requires all-to-one connectivity.\n"
"To avoid this, further optimization is possible by replacing the controlled time-evolution gate with a control-free version, exploiting the symmetry of the Hamiltonian.\n"
"Let's observe the following circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dans le test de swap étendu, contrôler l'évolution temporelle avec un seul qubit ancilla exige que l'ancilla contrôle de nombreuses portes à travers le système.\n"
"Cela peut introduire une surcharge de routage substantielle et, dans le pire des cas, nécessite effectivement une connectivité de tous vers un.\n"
"Pour éviter cela, une optimisation supplémentaire est possible en remplaçant la porte d'évolution temporelle contrôlée par une version sans contrôle, en exploitant la symétrie du hamiltonien.\n"
"Observons le circuit suivant.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![circuit optimization](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/circuit_opt.avif)\n"
msgstr "![circuit optimization](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/circuit_opt.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, $B_{\\rm ref}$ prepares the reference state, $B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle = |\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Ici, $B_{\\rm ref}$ prépare l'état de référence, $B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle = |\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead of first preparing $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)|\\psi_0\\rangle$ and then applying $U(t)$ only on the $|1\\rangle$ branch, the circuit directly prepares the two branches as\n"
msgstr "Au lieu de préparer d'abord $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)|\\psi_0\\rangle$ puis d'appliquer $U(t)$ uniquement sur la branche $|1\\rangle$, le circuit prépare directement les deux branches comme\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\quad \\text{and} \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\quad \\text{and} \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where\n"
msgstr "where\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_d\\rangle = U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_d\\rangle = U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit first applies a Hadamard gate to the ancilla and prepares the reference state only on the $|1\\rangle$ branch:\n"
msgstr "Le circuit applique d'abord une porte de Hadamard à l'ancilla et prépare l'état de référence uniquement sur la branche $|1\\rangle$ :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then the uncontrolled time-evolution operator is applied to both branches:\n"
msgstr "Ensuite, l'opérateur d'évolution temporelle non contrôlé est appliqué aux deux branches :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since the Hamiltonian preserves the excitation number, we can see that $|0^n\\rangle$ is its eigenstate, and thus\n"
"the evolution operator only accumulates a phase under the Hamiltonian:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t)|0^n\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Étant donné que le hamiltonien préserve le nombre d'excitations, nous pouvons voir que $|0^n\\rangle$ en est l'état propre, et donc\n"
"l'opérateur d'évolution n'accumule qu'une phase sous le hamiltonien :\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t)|0^n\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0^n\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0^n\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Therefore,\n"
msgstr "Therefore,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, $B_{\\rm ref}$ is applied only on the $|0\\rangle$ branch.\n"
msgstr "Ensuite, $B_{\\rm ref}$ est appliqué uniquement sur la branche $|0\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At this point, the two branches have an extra relative phase. To remove it, we apply the ancilla phase gate\n"
msgstr "À ce stade, les deux branches ont une phase relative supplémentaire. Pour la supprimer, nous appliquons la porte de phase de l'ancilla\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"P(-E_{\\rm vac}t)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"P(-E_{\\rm vac}t)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This transforms the state as\n"
msgstr "Cela transforme l'état comme\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, up to an irrelevant global phase, we finally prepared\n"
msgstr "Ainsi, à une phase globale non pertinente près, nous avons finalement préparé\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the next code block, we implement this control-free circuit.\n"
msgstr "Dans le prochain bloc de code, nous implémentons ce circuit sans contrôle.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/790e5e0c-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/790e5e0c-1.avif)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpilation {#transpilation}"
msgstr "Transpilation {#transpilation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, we transpile the controlled- and control-free circuits to become executable on the hardware.\n"
"Let's compare the result of the transpiled circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nous transpilons maintenant les circuits contrôlé et sans contrôle pour les rendre exécutables sur le matériel.\n"
"Comparons le résultat des circuits transpilés.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Étape 3 : Exécuter à l'aide des primitives Qiskit {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The next step is to submit the same parameterized circuit for several values of $d$. For each $d$, we estimate four expectation values: $X\\otimes I$, $Y\\otimes I$, $X\\otimes (H-T)$, and $Y\\otimes (H-T)$. These four numbers are then combined into the complex first-row elements $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}$ and $\\mathcal{H}_{0d}$.\n"
msgstr "L'étape suivante consiste à soumettre le même circuit paramétré pour plusieurs valeurs de $d$. Pour chaque $d$, nous estimons quatre valeurs d'espérance : $X\\otimes I$, $Y\\otimes I$, $X\\otimes (H-T)$ et $Y\\otimes (H-T)$. Ces quatre nombres sont ensuite combinés en les éléments complexes de première ligne $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}$ et $\\mathcal{H}_{0d}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, $\\mathcal{S}_{00}=1$ and $\\mathcal{H}_{00}=\\langle\\psi_{0}|(H-T)|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\langle\\psi_{0}|H|\\psi_{0}\\rangle-\\tau$ can be classically calculated since $\\lvert\\psi_0\\rangle$ is sparse, so we skip the $d=0$ case.\n"
msgstr "Ici, $\\mathcal{S}_{00}=1$ et $\\mathcal{H}_{00}=\\langle\\psi_{0}|(H-T)|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\langle\\psi_{0}|H|\\psi_{0}\\rangle-\\tau$ peuvent être calculés classiquement puisque $\\lvert\\psi_0\\rangle$ est creux, nous ignorons donc le cas $d=0$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Étape 4 : Post-traitement et renvoi du résultat dans le format classique souhaité {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After estimating the projected matrices, we regularize and solve the GEVP\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c} = E\\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"The smallest generalized eigenvalue gives the KQD estimate of the ground-state energy.\n"
msgstr ""
"Après avoir estimé les matrices projetées, nous régularisons et résolvons le GEVP\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c} = E\\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"La plus petite valeur propre généralisée donne l'estimation KQD de l'énergie de l'état fondamental.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we solve the generalized eigenvalue problem using the matrices reconstructed from the circuit estimates.\n"
"In an ideal statevector calculation with exact real-time evolution, this should reproduce the exact projected result.\n"
"In practice, deviations can come from Trotterization, sampling error, and numerical instability of the overlap matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nous résolvons maintenant le problème aux valeurs propres généralisé en utilisant les matrices reconstruites à partir des estimations des circuits.\n"
"Dans un calcul idéal de vecteur d'état avec évolution en temps réel exacte, cela devrait reproduire le résultat projeté exact.\n"
"En pratique, les écarts peuvent provenir de la trotterisation, de l'erreur d'échantillonnage et de l'instabilité numérique de la matrice de recouvrement.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We observe how the energy converges as we increase the dimension of the Krylov subspace.\n"
msgstr "Nous observons comment l'énergie converge à mesure que nous augmentons la dimension du sous-espace de Krylov.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/08d57f33-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/08d57f33-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Exemple de matériel à grande échelle {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The previous section used a 12-qubit model so that the statevector simulation could be used as a diagnostic. We now scale the same KQD workflow to a 30-qubit Heisenberg chain and prepare the workload for execution on IBM Quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr "La section précédente utilisait un modèle à 12 qubits afin que la simulation de vecteur d'état puisse servir de diagnostic. Nous passons maintenant à l'échelle le même flux de travail KQD à une chaîne de Heisenberg à 30 qubits et préparons la charge de travail pour l'exécution sur du matériel IBM Quantum.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 1-4 compressed into a single code block {#steps-1-4-compressed-into-a-single-code-block}"
msgstr "Étapes 1 à 4 compressées en un seul bloc de code {#steps-1-4-compressed-into-a-single-code-block}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we now put all of these details together into a singular workflow at a larger scale, which is then run on our real quantum hardware. In this section, we apply realistic error-mitigation settings to improve the reliability of the results. Since the matrix elements corresponding to different values of $d$ can be evaluated in parallel, we use `Batch` mode to execute them efficiently.\n"
msgstr "Nous rassemblons maintenant tous ces détails dans un flux de travail unique à plus grande échelle, qui est ensuite exécuté sur notre matériel quantique réel. Dans cette section, nous appliquons des paramètres réalistes d'atténuation d'erreur pour améliorer la fiabilité des résultats. Étant donné que les éléments de matrice correspondant à différentes valeurs de $d$ peuvent être évalués en parallèle, nous utilisons le mode `Batch` pour les exécuter efficacement.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/e3e0d1f3-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/e3e0d1f3-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Appendix: The Hamiltonian-function (spectral-filter) viewpoint {#appendix-the-hamiltonian-function-spectral-filter-viewpoint}"
msgstr "Annexe : le point de vue de la fonction-hamiltonienne (filtre spectral) {#appendix-the-hamiltonian-function-spectral-filter-viewpoint}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The main workflow presented KQD operationally: build a Krylov basis from real-time-evolved states, estimate the projected matrices $\\mathcal{H}$ and $\\mathcal{S}$, and solve the GEVP.\n"
"This appendix revisits the *same* computation from a complementary angle that explains **why** KQD works: the *Hamiltonian-function*, or *spectral-filter*, viewpoint [\\[3\\]](#references), [\\[5\\]](#references).\n"
"It reuses the 12-qubit model, time step $\\Delta t$, and the Krylov solution already obtained above; no new circuit execution is required.\n"
msgstr ""
"Le flux de travail principal a présenté KQD de manière opérationnelle : construire une base de Krylov à partir d'états évolués en temps réel, estimer les matrices projetées $\\mathcal{H}$ et $\\mathcal{S}$, et résoudre le GEVP.\n"
"Cette annexe revisite le *même* calcul sous un angle complémentaire qui explique **pourquoi** KQD fonctionne : le point de vue de la *fonction-hamiltonienne*, ou du *filtre spectral* [\\[3\\]](#references), [\\[5\\]](#references).\n"
"Elle réutilise le modèle à 12 qubits, le pas de temps $\\Delta t$, et la solution de Krylov déjà obtenue ci-dessus ; aucune nouvelle exécution de circuit n'est requise.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reference state as an energy distribution {#the-reference-state-as-an-energy-distribution}"
msgstr "L'état de référence comme distribution d'énergie {#the-reference-state-as-an-energy-distribution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let the Hamiltonian have the eigendecomposition\n"
msgstr "Soit le hamiltonien ayant la décomposition en valeurs propres\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H=\\sum_{m} E_m\\,|E_m\\rangle\\!\\langle E_m|,\n"
"\\qquad E_0\\le E_1\\le\\cdots,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H=\\sum_{m} E_m\\,|E_m\\rangle\\!\\langle E_m|,\n"
"\\qquad E_0\\le E_1\\le\\cdots,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"with energy eigenstates $|E_m\\rangle$.\n"
"Any reference state can be expanded in this eigenbasis,\n"
msgstr ""
"avec des états propres d'énergie $|E_m\\rangle$.\n"
"Tout état de référence peut être développé dans cette base propre,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\sum_m a_m\\,|E_m\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad a_m=\\langle E_m|\\psi_{0}\\rangle,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\sum_m a_m\\,|E_m\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad a_m=\\langle E_m|\\psi_{0}\\rangle,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"so it carries a **spectral weight** $p_m=|a_m|^2$ at each energy $E_m$.\n"
"The reference energy is the mean of this distribution, $\\langle H\\rangle_{0}=\\sum_m p_m E_m$.\n"
msgstr ""
"il porte donc un **poids spectral** $p_m=|a_m|^2$ à chaque énergie $E_m$.\n"
"L'énergie de référence est la moyenne de cette distribution, $\\langle H\\rangle_{0}=\\sum_m p_m E_m$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The eigendecomposition of a general $n$-qubit Hamiltonian is exponentially costly, so this picture is only a diagnostic, which is *not* part of the algorithm.\n"
"Here, however, we can compute it cheaply for the *same* $n=12$ problem: the Heisenberg Hamiltonian conserves the total excitation number, and the reference $|000001000000\\rangle$ carries a single excitation, so its entire spectral content lives in the single-excitation subspace whose dimension grows only linearly with $n$.\n"
"We therefore reuse the exact single-excitation block (already used above as a benchmark) and read off the reference distribution $\\{(E_m, p_m)\\}$ inside that subspace.\n"
msgstr ""
"La décomposition en valeurs propres d'un hamiltonien général à $n$ qubits est exponentiellement coûteuse, donc cette image n'est qu'un diagnostic, qui ne fait *pas* partie de l'algorithme.\n"
"Ici, cependant, nous pouvons la calculer à moindre coût pour le *même* problème $n=12$ : le hamiltonien de Heisenberg conserve le nombre total d'excitations, et la référence $|000001000000\\rangle$ porte une seule excitation, de sorte que tout son contenu spectral se trouve dans le sous-espace à excitation unique dont la dimension croît uniquement de manière linéaire avec $n$.\n"
"Nous réutilisons donc le bloc exact à excitation unique (déjà utilisé ci-dessus comme référence) et lisons la distribution de référence $\\{(E_m, p_m)\\}$ dans ce sous-espace.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "KQD learns a filter that reshapes this distribution {#kqd-learns-a-filter-that-reshapes-this-distribution}"
msgstr "KQD apprend un filtre qui remodèle cette distribution {#kqd-learns-a-filter-that-reshapes-this-distribution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **Hamiltonian function** $f(H)$ is defined through spectral calculus,\n"
msgstr "Une **fonction-hamiltonienne** $f(H)$ est définie par le calcul spectral,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"f(H)=\\sum_m f(E_m)\\,|E_m\\rangle\\!\\langle E_m|,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"f(H)=\\sum_m f(E_m)\\,|E_m\\rangle\\!\\langle E_m|,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"or in other words, a weighted sum of eigenprojectors.\n"
"Applying it to the reference reshapes each spectral amplitude, $a_m \\to a_m f(E_m)$:\n"
msgstr ""
"ou, en d'autres termes, une somme pondérée de projecteurs propres.\n"
"Son application à la référence remodèle chaque amplitude spectrale, $a_m \\to a_m f(E_m)$ :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"f(H)\\,|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\sum_m a_m\\,f(E_m)\\,|E_m\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"f(H)\\,|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\sum_m a_m\\,f(E_m)\\,|E_m\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $f$ were sharply peaked at the lowest energy ($f(E_0)=1$ and $f(E_m)\\approx 0$ otherwise) then $f(H)$ would act as a ground-state projector, and the normalized output would be (close to) the ground state.\n"
"Therefore, a good low-pass **spectral filter** in energy is exactly what we want.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si $f$ était fortement piqué à l'énergie la plus basse ($f(E_0)=1$ et $f(E_m)\\approx 0$ sinon), alors $f(H)$ agirait comme un projecteur d'état fondamental, et la sortie normalisée serait (proche de) l'état fondamental.\n"
"Par conséquent, un bon **filtre spectral** passe-bas en énergie est exactement ce que nous voulons.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "KQD does not prescribe $f$ in advance. Instead it expands the filter in the real-time-evolution basis,\n"
msgstr "KQD ne prescrit pas $f$ à l'avance. Il développe plutôt le filtre dans la base d'évolution en temps réel,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"f_{\\rm KQD}(E)=\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell\\, e^{-i\\ell\\Delta t E},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"f_{\\rm KQD}(E)=\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell\\, e^{-i\\ell\\Delta t E},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"a *trigonometric* function of the energy whose coefficients $\\{c_\\ell\\}$ are precisely the GEVP eigenvector solved for above.\n"
"Minimizing the Rayleigh quotient $\\mathbf{c}^\\dagger\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c}/\\mathbf{c}^\\dagger\\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}$ is therefore the same as *learning* the filter that best suppresses the excited-state weight of the reference.\n"
"Larger Krylov dimension $r$ gives the filter more degrees of freedom and a sharper peak at the ground-state energy.\n"
msgstr ""
"une fonction *trigonométrique* de l'énergie dont les coefficients $\\{c_\\ell\\}$ sont précisément le vecteur propre du GEVP résolu ci-dessus.\n"
"Minimiser le quotient de Rayleigh $\\mathbf{c}^\\dagger\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c}/\\mathbf{c}^\\dagger\\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}$ revient donc à *apprendre* le filtre qui supprime le mieux le poids des états excités de la référence.\n"
"Une dimension de Krylov $r$ plus grande donne au filtre plus de degrés de liberté et un pic plus net à l'énergie de l'état fondamental.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The helper below evaluates this learned filter on an energy axis; we then apply it to the reference distribution obtained above.\n"
msgstr "La fonction d'aide ci-dessous évalue ce filtre appris sur un axe d'énergie ; nous l'appliquons ensuite à la distribution de référence obtenue ci-dessus.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize the filter and its flexibility {#visualize-the-filter-and-its-flexibility}"
msgstr "Visualiser le filtre et sa flexibilité {#visualize-the-filter-and-its-flexibility}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We first show the learned filter at the full Krylov dimension used above, then track how it sharpens as the dimension $r$ grows.\n"
msgstr "Nous montrons d'abord le filtre appris à la dimension de Krylov complète utilisée ci-dessus, puis nous suivons comment il s'affine à mesure que la dimension $r$ augmente.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bars show the reference spectral weights $p_m$ (before) and the filtered weights $p_m|f_{\\rm KQD}(E_m)|^2$ (after), together with the learned filter intensity $|f_{\\rm KQD}(E)|^2$ on a continuous energy axis.\n"
"The filter concentrates the weight onto the lowest energy of the single-excitation subspace &mdash; the same energy that the KQD estimate converged to in the small-scale example.\n"
"Note that this is the ground state *within the single-excitation sector*, which is the relevant target for this excitation-conserving reference state, not the global ground state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Les barres montrent les poids spectraux de référence $p_m$ (avant) et les poids filtrés $p_m|f_{\\rm KQD}(E_m)|^2$ (après), avec l'intensité du filtre appris $|f_{\\rm KQD}(E)|^2$ sur un axe d'énergie continu.\n"
"Le filtre concentre le poids sur l'énergie la plus basse du sous-espace à excitation unique &mdash; la même énergie vers laquelle l'estimation KQD a convergé dans l'exemple à petite échelle.\n"
"Note qu'il s'agit de l'état fondamental *au sein du secteur à excitation unique*, qui est la cible pertinente pour cet état de référence conservant l'excitation, et non de l'état fondamental global.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/app-code-plot-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/app-code-plot-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Increasing the Krylov dimension: flexibility of the learned function {#increasing-the-krylov-dimension-flexibility-of-the-learned-function}"
msgstr "Augmenter la dimension de Krylov : flexibilité de la fonction apprise {#increasing-the-krylov-dimension-flexibility-of-the-learned-function}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recall that the learned filter is a trigonometric polynomial in the energy with $r$ coefficients,\n"
msgstr "Rappelons que le filtre appris est un polynôme trigonométrique en énergie avec $r$ coefficients,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"f_{\\rm KQD}(E)=\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell\\, e^{-i\\ell\\Delta t E}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"f_{\\rm KQD}(E)=\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell\\, e^{-i\\ell\\Delta t E}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Krylov dimension $r$ is exactly the number of free coefficients, so it controls the **flexibility** of the function.\n"
"A small $r$ can only produce a broad, gently varying filter that leaks weight into low-lying excited states; when $r$ increases, the filter can form a narrower peak at the target energy and suppress the remaining excited-state weight more aggressively.\n"
"This is the spectral-filter counterpart of the energy convergence observed in the small-scale example: as $r$ grows, the filtered distribution collapses onto the subspace ground state and the estimated energy decreases toward it.\n"
msgstr ""
"La dimension de Krylov $r$ est exactement le nombre de coefficients libres, elle contrôle donc la **flexibilité** de la fonction.\n"
"Un petit $r$ ne peut produire qu'un filtre large et variant doucement qui laisse fuir du poids vers les états excités de basse énergie ; lorsque $r$ augmente, le filtre peut former un pic plus étroit à l'énergie cible et supprimer plus agressivement le poids restant des états excités.\n"
"C'est le pendant en filtre spectral de la convergence d'énergie observée dans l'exemple à petite échelle : à mesure que $r$ augmente, la distribution filtrée s'effondre vers l'état fondamental du sous-espace et l'énergie estimée diminue vers celui-ci.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We reuse the projected matrices already estimated above and simply solve the GEVP at each leading $r\\times r$ block, then evaluate and plot the corresponding filter.\n"
msgstr "Nous réutilisons les matrices projetées déjà estimées ci-dessus et résolvons simplement le GEVP à chaque bloc principal $r\\times r$, puis évaluons et traçons le filtre correspondant.\n"

